# ---------- Secrets ----------
# Everything that looks like an environment file is ignored, and the templates
# are named back in one at a time. A new .env.<something> is therefore ignored
# by default, which is the right way round: the cost of forgetting to ignore a
# real one is a published credential.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
*.pem
*.key

